-- title:
--   Level lowering to the unit-root corner ring across Nr ∣ Nrp
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal O$ is a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k =$ `ResidueField 𝒪`, and $p$ is a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ (hypothesis `hp𝒪`).
--
--   **Residual representation.** $\bar\rho$ is a [`ResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L22) over $k$: a $k$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (realised as $\overline{\mathbb Q} \simeq_{\mathbb Q} \overline{\mathbb Q}$, where $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) to $\mathrm{End}_k(V)$ which is trivial on the absolute Galois group of some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. It is assumed absolutely irreducible (`habs`: after base change to an algebraic closure of $k$, every Galois-stable submodule is $\bot$ or $\top$), and ordinary at $p$ (`hord`, for the associated [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16)): for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $P$ there is a submodule $L \subseteq V$ spanned by one member of a two-element basis, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$, and such that $\bar\rho(\sigma)v - v \in L$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ and all $v \in V$.
--
--   **Levels and the auxiliary prime.** $S$ is a finite set of primes (`hS`) containing $p$ (`hpS`); $N$ is a non-zero natural number with $p \nmid N$ (`hpN`) all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$ (`hNS`). A subset $S_{\min} \subseteq S$ containing $p$ is given with: `hmin`, for primes $q \neq p$, $q \in S_{\min}$ precisely when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (i.e. not every inertia element at $q$ acts trivially); `hNmin`, every $q \in S_{\min}$ with $q \neq p$ divides $N$; `hNunr`, every prime $q \neq p$ outside $S_{\min}$ dividing $N$ has $q^2 \mid N$; `htame`, for $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ on $V$. Further, $r$ is a prime with $r \geq 5$, $r \notin S$, $r \nmid Np$ and $p \nmid r-1$, subject to the trace condition `hrρ`: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $r$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$, $\mathrm{tr}(\bar\rho(\sigma))^2 \neq (r+1)^2$ in $k$.
--
--   **Eigensystems and $\mathcal O$-points.** The weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(Np)$ and for $\Gamma_0(N)$ are assumed to have integral structure (their lattices of forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients span over $\mathbb C$). Here `heckeAlgebra M 2 S` is the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(M)))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$ and the $U_q$ with $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$. Ring homomorphisms $\theta_1 : \mathbb T(Np) \to k$ and $\theta_0 : \mathbb T(N) \to k$ are given which cut out $\bar\rho$ (`hθ₁`, `hθ₀`): for every prime $\ell \notin S$ not dividing $Np$ (respectively $N$), every valuation subring over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ there, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2 - \theta_i(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Write `heckeLocal M S 𝒪 θ` for the localisation of the $\mathcal O$-base change of the integral Hecke lattice at the prime determined by $\theta$, and `heckeLocal.π` for the canonical map from `heckeAlgebra M 2 S` into it. Given are $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms $\pi_{T_0} : \mathbb T(N)_{\theta_0} \to \mathcal O$ and $\pi_{T_1} : \mathbb T(Np)_{\theta_1} \to \mathcal O$ agreeing on Hecke operators away from the level (`hπ`: for primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid Np$ and $\ell \nmid N$, $\pi_{T_1}(T_\ell) = \pi_{T_0}(T_\ell)$).
--
--   **The cohomological datum at level $Nr$.** $H_0 \leq (\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$ (`hH₀`). The carrier is $H^1(Nr, H_0, \mathcal O)$, the additive homomorphisms from the group $\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)$ (the elements of $\Gamma_0(Nr)$ whose lower-right entry reduces into $H_0$), written additively, to $\mathcal O$. A commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $\mathbb T_0$ acts on this carrier compatibly with $\mathcal O$; $S_0$ is an `IdempotentSplitting` of $\mathbb T_0$ (a finite family of complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals, with $e_i \in \mathfrak m_j$ iff $i \neq j$), $i_0$ an index, and $e_0$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism from the corner ring $e_{i_0}\mathbb T_0 e_{i_0}$ onto $\mathbb T(N)_{\theta_0}$; the corner module $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1(Nr,H_0,\mathcal O)$ is finite and free over $\mathcal O$. An element $t_p$ of the corner ring is given. The hypotheses on this datum are: `hT₀`, for primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \nmid Nr$, the element $e_0^{-1}(\pi(T_\ell))$ acts on the corner module as the operator `heckeT (N * r) H₀ ℓ 𝒪`; `htp` (three clauses), $t_p$ is a unit and acts on the corner module both as `heckeT (N * r) H₀ p 𝒪` and as `heckeTlower (N * r) H₀ p 𝒪`; `hocc₀`, the submodule of the corner module annihilated by $\ker(\pi_{T_0} \circ e_0)$ is non-zero; `hrk₀`, the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner module equals the $\mathcal O$-rank of that annihilated submodule times the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner ring; `hgen`, every element of $\mathbb T_0$ acts on $H^1(Nr,H_0,\mathcal O)$ through the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of endomorphisms generated by the family [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) (the operators $T_\ell$, $U_q$ and the diamond operators indexed by `Gen (N * r) S`); `tfull` together with `htfull` and `cfull` together with `hcfull`, for every generator $g$ which is not of the form $U_q$ with $q \nmid N$, an element $\mathrm{tfull}(g) \in \mathbb T_0$ acting as `opFamily … g` and a scalar $\mathrm{cfull}(g) \in \mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{tfull}(g) - \mathrm{cfull}(g) \in \mathfrak m_{i_0}$; `hcofull`, any $v$ in the carrier lies in the corner module as soon as for each such $g$ and each $k$ some power $(\mathrm{tfull}(g) - \mathrm{cfull}(g))^n$ carries $v$ into $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k \cdot H^1(Nr,H_0,\mathcal O)$; `hfaith₀`, the corner ring acts faithfully on the corner module; `hdia`, every $\sigma \in \Gamma_0(Nr)$ acts trivially on the corner module through `diamondRaw` (precomposition with conjugation by $\sigma$). Finally $\tilde\alpha$ is an element of the corner ring satisfying `hαt` (three clauses): $\tilde\alpha$ is a unit, $\tilde\alpha^2 - t_p\tilde\alpha + p = 0$, and $\tilde\alpha - t_p$ lies in the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$; that is, $\tilde\alpha$ is the unit root of $X^2 - t_pX + p$.
--
--   **The datum at level $Nrp$.** $H \leq (\mathbb Z/Nrp)^\times$ is the preimage of $H_0$ (`hH`). Two commutative $\mathcal O$-algebras $\mathbb T_a$, $\mathbb T_1$, each module-finite over $\mathcal O$, act on $H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$ compatibly with $\mathcal O$; $\iota : \mathbb T_a \to \mathbb T_1$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra map compatible with the two actions (`hι`), $U \in \mathbb T_1$ acts as `heckeT (N * r * p) H p 𝒪` (`hU`), and $\mathbb T_1$ is generated over $\mathcal O$ by the image of $\iota$ together with $U$ (`hgen₁`). Idempotent splittings $S_a$ of $\mathbb T_a$ with index $i_a$ and $S_1$ of $\mathbb T_1$ with index $i_1$ are given, $e_1$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism from $e_{i_1}\mathbb T_1e_{i_1}$ onto $\mathbb T(Np)_{\theta_1}$, and both corner modules $e_{i_a}\cdot H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$, $e_{i_1}\cdot H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$ are finite and free over $\mathcal O$. A level datum $h_{1a} :$ `LevelLE (N*r*p) (N*r*p) ⊤ H 1` is given (divisibility of levels, $1$ dividing the quotient, and compatibility of the character groups), together with maps $t_A$ from `Gen (N * r) S` to $\mathbb T_a$ and $d_A$ from $(\mathbb Z/Nrp)^\times$ to $\mathbb T_a$. The hypothesis `hE` is a conjunction of fifteen clauses, each listed here: (i) for every generator $g$ that is either some $T_\ell$ or some $U_q$ with $q \mid N$ (diamond generators being excluded by the guard), $t_A(g)$ acts on $H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$ as the operator `heckeT (N * r * p) H · 𝒪` at the corresponding prime; (ii) for those $g$, $t_A(g) - \mathrm{cfull}(g) \in \mathfrak m_{i_a}$; (iii) each $d_A(d)$ acts as `diamondL (N * r * p) H 𝒪 d`; (iv) $d_A(d) - 1 \in \mathfrak m_{i_a}$ for all $d$; (v) the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathbb T_a$ generated by the $t_A(g)$ for those $g$ together with the image of $d_A$ is all of $\mathbb T_a$; (vi) every element of the $S_a$-corner module lies in the image, under the degeneracy map `iDegL` attached to $h_{1a}$, of the submodule of parabolic homomorphisms (those vanishing on elements of trace square $4$); (vii) $\iota^{-1}(\mathfrak m_{i_1}) = \mathfrak m_{i_a}$; (viii) $U \notin \mathfrak m_{i_1}$; (ix) for $a \in \mathcal O$, if $\tilde\alpha - a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $e_{i_0}\mathbb T_0e_{i_0}$ then $U - a \in \mathfrak m_{i_1}$; (x) the $S_1$-corner module is contained in the $S_a$-corner module; (xi) there is a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi$ from $e_{i_a}\mathbb T_ae_{i_a}$ onto $e_{i_1}\mathbb T_1e_{i_1}$ compatible with the two actions on elements of the carrier that coincide, and such that for primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid Np$ and $\ell \nmid Nrp$ the element $e_1^{-1}(\pi(T_\ell))$ acts on the $S_1$-corner module as `heckeT (N * r * p) H ℓ 𝒪`; (xii) $e_{i_1}\mathbb T_1e_{i_1}$ acts faithfully on its corner module; (xiii) the submodule of that corner module annihilated by $\ker(\pi_{T_1}\circ e_1)$ is non-zero; (xiv) the $\mathcal O$-rank of that corner module equals the rank of the annihilated submodule times the rank of the corner ring; (xv) the saturation statement that for $a \in \mathcal O$ non-zero and $m'$ in the corner module, $a\,m' \in \ker(\pi_{T_1}\circ e_1)\cdot(\text{corner module})$ implies $m' \in \ker(\pi_{T_1}\circ e_1)\cdot(\text{corner module})$.
--
--   **Degeneracy hypotheses.** Level data $h_1 :$ `LevelLE (N*r) (N*r*p) H₀ H 1` and $h_p :$ `LevelLE (N*r) (N*r*p) H₀ H p` are given, and with $\iota_1^{*}, \iota_p^{*}$ the corresponding degeneracy maps `iDegL` from $H^1(Nr,H_0,\mathcal O)$ to $H^1(Nrp,H,\mathcal O)$: `hLa`, both $\iota_1^{*}$ and $\iota_p^{*}$ (indexed by $k \in \mathrm{Fin}\,2$) carry the $S_0$-corner module into the $S_a$-corner module; `hLc`, for every $m$ in the $S_0$-corner module, $\iota_1^{*}(\tilde\alpha\, m) - \iota_p^{*}(m)$ lies in the $S_1$-corner module.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exists an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_1$ from $e_{i_1}\mathbb T_1e_{i_1}$ to $e_{i_0}\mathbb T_0e_{i_0}$ such that: (1) $\mathrm{res}_1$ is surjective; (2) $\pi_{T_1}\circ e_1 = (\pi_{T_0}\circ e_0)\circ\mathrm{res}_1$, so the $\mathcal O$-point upstairs factors through $\mathrm{res}_1$; (3) for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid Np$ and $\ell \nmid N$, $\mathrm{res}_1\big(e_1^{-1}(\pi_{Np}(T_\ell))\big) = e_0^{-1}(\pi_N(T_\ell))$; (4) $\mathrm{res}_1$ sends the image of $U$ under the corner projection $\mathbb T_1 \to e_{i_1}\mathbb T_1e_{i_1}$ to $\tilde\alpha$; (5) the $\mathcal O$-rank of the submodule of the $S_1$-corner module annihilated by $\ker(\pi_{T_1}\circ e_1)$ equals the $\mathcal O$-rank of the submodule of the $S_0$-corner module annihilated by $\ker(\pi_{T_0}\circ e_0)$ (both regarded as $\mathcal O$-modules by restriction of scalars); and (6) for every prime $q$ dividing $Nr$ and dividing $N$, the element $\mathrm{res}_1$ applied to the corner projection of $\iota(t_A(U_q))$ acts on the $S_0$-corner module as the operator `heckeT (N * r) H₀ q 𝒪`.
--
--   This is the level-lowering half of the Hecke-side comparison across the rung $Nr \mid Nrp$: classically, restriction of the ordinary local component of the Hecke algebra of level $Nrp$ (where $U_p$ is a unit) to the $\tilde\alpha$-stabilised old subspace $\iota_1^{*}\tilde\alpha - \iota_p^{*}$, on which $U_p$ acts through the unit root $\tilde\alpha$ of $X^2 - T_pX + p$. It is used in the assembly of the relative two-level corner datum, [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_refinement_degeneracy_level_mul_of_cornerData_of_fullCorner_of_trace_sq_ne_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_refinement_degeneracy_level_mul_of_cornerData_of_fullCorner_of_trace_sq_ne_of_not_cube_dvd).
